6. A common mistake: the max() of every column
========================================================================
+----------+-------------------+---------------+---------+
|package_id|scan_time          |location       |status   |
+----------+-------------------+---------------+---------+
|PKG-1001  |2026-10-21 14:32:00|Santa Clara, CA|picked up|
|PKG-1002  |2026-10-22 03:10:00|Seattle, WA    |picked up|
|PKG-1003  |2026-10-22 18:20:00|Dallas, TX     |picked up|
+----------+-------------------+---------------+---------+

Every package is now 'picked up', and PKG-1002 is in Seattle at
03:10 on 10-22: a scan that never happened (it was in Portland).
Columns that must come from the SAME row must travel together: in
one struct, with max_by(), or with a window. (Similarly, F.last()
is 'the last one wins': non-deterministic after a shuffle.)
